Faxbot: lossless tuning of the page coding faxsend sends (HylaFAX+ 7.0.11).

The receiver decodes exactly the pixels it would have got without this patch;
only how they are coded changes. faxd/LosslessTuning.h explains both choices.

MR: every page sent in MR is coded with the fewest-bytes legal reset
schedule (T.4 4.2.1.3.4 allows a one-dimensional line earlier than every K
lines), chosen by dynamic programming over each row's measured one- and
two-dimensional code lengths, with this encoder's EOL alignment and, without
ECM, the minimum scan line fill Class1Send adds. An MR file is coded again
even when the session is MR too (Class1Send/Class2Send), so the tuned
schedule is never skipped, and faxsend keeps a data format the job asked
for itself (DesiredDF, measured by Faxbot) instead of switching MR or MMR
to MH whenever tiff2fax's MH file is smaller than its MMR file
(FaxSend.c++). TuneMR (default yes) turns the schedule off.

JBIG: the page is encoded with each of 12 T.85 settings (options 0, TPBON,
LRLTWO, both; MX 0, 8, 32; L0 128) and the smallest BIE goes, ties to the
lower options, then the lower MX. TuneJBIG: "sslfax" (default) tunes only
pages that go over SSL Fax, whose receiver is HylaFAX+ and decodes JBIG with
jbigkit's full decoder; "always" or "never" (Faxbot's job controls set them
per job). Plain JBIG stays options 0, MX 0.

Each converted page logs one "LOSSLESS TUNING" line in the session log
(settings, bytes, conversion time and the SHA-256 of the raster coded), which
Faxbot reads (hylafax/bin/negotiation). Tested at build time by
tests/lossless_tuning_test.c++.

